; A highlighter may answer for a range alone, and in pieces: the job
; sets each piece as it comes, so keys run between pieces, and takes
; newer edits between them. Here each answer is one line, and waits for
; a gate the test opens.
> (define p (pieces-buffer "p" "#a b\n#c d\n#e f\n"))
> (open-gate! p 1)
> (faces p)
(("#a" comment))
; This line runs while the job waits to answer for the second line, and
; its edit reaches the job after that answer.
> (buffers:insert! p 2 "x")
3
> (open-gate! p 2)
> (faces p)
(("#xa" comment) ("#c" comment))
; The next answer is told the edit and starts again from the first
; line; the spans outside its range stay.
> (open-gate! p 3)
> (faces p)
(("#xa" comment) ("#c" comment))
> (open-gate! p 4)
> (open-gate! p 5)
> (faces p)
(("#xa" comment) ("#c" comment) ("#e" comment))
> (marks:inputs)
(("p" #f) ("p" (1 0 ())) ("p" (2 1 ())) ("p" (3 0 ((1 0 1)))) ("p" (4 1 ())) ("p" (5 2 ())))
; When the buffer's log no longer holds the version an answer was
; computed for, the job sends every span it holds again, moved to its
; newest version: here the answer for the second line, computed before
; a thousand and one lines were added above it.
> (define q (pieces-buffer "q" "#a\n#b\n#c\n"))
> (open-gate! q 1)
> (faces q)
(("#a" comment))
> (do ([i 0 (+ i 1)]) ((= i 1001)) (buffers:insert! q 1 "\n"))
; Logs are trimmed to their last thousand edits after a second idle.
> (begin (set-idle! #t) (sleep-for 1.5) (set-idle! #f))
> (buffers:edits-since q 0)
#f
> (open-gate! q 2)
> (open-gate! q 3)
> (faces q)
(("#a" comment) ("#b" comment))
; A ranged answer is cut to its range: of spans reaching outside it, only
; their part inside is set.
> (define r (marked "r" "#abcd #ef\n" marks:ranged))
> (buffers:with-buffer r (set-option-local! marks:range '(0 3)))
> (syntax-highlighting:update! r)
> (faces r)
(("#ab" comment))
> (buffers:with-buffer r (set-option-local! marks:range '(4 8)))
> (syntax-highlighting:update! r)
> (faces r)
(("#ab" comment) ("d" comment) ("#e" comment))
